      "content": "thanks for the advice. it's just so targeted though. like, the cafeteria thing wasn't an accident, they know my medical records from when i joined. and the payroll thing? my manager was the one who \"forgot\" to hit send on the update. it's all so calculated. do you think there's a specific way i should frame these in my log so they can't claim it was just \"coincidence\" or \"administrative error\" later?",
